WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.248
If you're a professional seller, you can receive two types of Amazon Business Fee Discounts when

00:00:07.248 --> 00:00:14.949
you offer business prices or quantity discounts of 3% or more off your standard price to business-

00:00:14.949 --> 00:00:18.120
to-business or B2B customers.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.120
Referral Fee Discounts and FBA Fulfillment Fee Discounts

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:27.280
Referral Fee Discounts reduce the percentage Amazon charges on each sale.

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:34.836
You can receive Referral Fee Discounts on bulk orders of a single product exceeding $1,000 for both

00:00:34.836 --> 00:00:39.280
Fulfillment by Amazon FBA and Fulfillment by Merchant FBM Orders.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:45.280
You pay the standard referral fee rate on the first $1,000 of the order value.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:51.280
For amounts above $1,000, you pay reduced rates that decrease as the order value increases.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:58.462
FBA Fulfillment Fee discounts lower the per-unit cost Amazon charges to pick, pack, and ship your

00:00:58.462 --> 00:01:02.280
products when business customers order multiple units.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:08.280
You can receive FBA Fulfillment Fee discounts on multi-unit orders of 2 or more.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:14.280
Your product must be fulfilled by Amazon and fall within eligible-size tiers for your marketplace.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:20.280
If eligible, when a business customer orders 2 or more units, you receive a per-unit fee reduction.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:26.280
The more units ordered, the greater the discount per unit.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:33.314
To qualify for fee discounts, set business prices or quantity discounts of at least 3% by applying

00:01:33.314 --> 00:01:38.280
discounts across your catalog using the business catalog rule in automate pricing.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:47.049
You can also manage business discounts through the B2B API, add products in bulk, or update business

00:01:47.049 --> 00:01:50.280
prices one by one through manage inventory.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:57.553
Use the business discounts insights or BDI tool to optimize your B2B prices using pricing insights

00:01:57.553 --> 00:01:58.280
and opportunities.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:07.189
Monitor your overall B2B performance in B2B Central and check whether your products fall into B2

00:02:07.189 --> 00:02:09.735
B relevant categories, like office products.

00:02:09.735 --> 00:02:12.280
Electronics or tools and home improvement.

00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:19.480
Leverage business reports B2B to dive deeper into sales and traffic data of business customers and

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:22.280
refine your B2B strategy further.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:28.959
To see if your referral fee discount or FBA Fulfillment Fee discount has been applied, access the

00:02:28.959 --> 00:02:33.280
payments dashboard in Seller Central and select the Transaction View tab.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:38.280
Select the order link to view transaction details, your discounts appear as.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:45.280
Discount on FBA per unit fulfillment fee or discount on referral fee for each qualifying order.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:51.566
For step-by-step instructions on how to set and optimize business pricing and quantity discounts,

00:02:51.566 --> 00:02:56.280
read the set business prices and quantity discounts guide in Seller University.
